T*
(How the Orvan grain corridor worked, and why its ending matters) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P1] The Corridor Agreement was a one-year arrangement signed on 10 September) Tj
T*
(2025. Asgard mediated it.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P2] Orvan grows more wheat and maize than it eats and sells the surplus by sea) Tj
T*
(from Orvan Grain Port. The agreement kept that sea route open to commercial) Tj
T*
(ships.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P3] Under the agreement, sea exports ran at about 95% of the old normal. The) Tj
T*
(deal covered wheat and maize leaving the port by sea; it did not cover rail) Tj
T*
(movements or sales by other exporters.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P4] The agreement expired on 10 September 2026. Talks on renewal failed, and) Tj
T*
(the port moved onto the general rules with no replacement arrangement.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P5] The main alternative is rail. The Ravik Rail Link can carry grain to Ravik) Tj
T*
(and onward, but its capacity is limited and it cannot move the volumes that the) Tj
T*
(sea route carried.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P6] Vanir also sells wheat, and some of that supply can reach Tolan and) Tj
T*
(Midgard. The amounts are small compared with Orvan's sea trade.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P7] Asgard holds a long-term wheat contract with Orvan. That contract is mostly) Tj
T*
(protected, which is why the Asgard wheat route behaves differently from the) Tj
T*
(open-market routes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P8] The agreement was unusual because it was not a tariff deal. It was a) Tj
T*
(shipping arrangement, brokered by a third country, that gave buyers a) Tj
T*
(predictable route and gave Orvan a reason to keep the port open. That made it) Tj
T*
(fragile: when the talks failed, there was no fallback rule to keep the ships) Tj
T*
(moving, and the strike turned a political lapse into an operational one. The) Tj
T*
(overland substitute is real, but it was never designed to carry the same volume.) Tj
T*
(That is why the event looks like a cliff followed by a partial recovery rather) Tj
T*
(than a simple shortage.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P9] The result is a cliff in sea volumes followed by a partial overland) Tj
T*
(substitute, not a full recovery.) Tj
T*
() Tj
